# Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Project Statement

{{.ProjectName}}

{{if .Scope}}Scope of this DEI.md file: {{.Scope}}.{{else}}Scope of this DEI.md file: this project and its community spaces.{{end}}

Our project prioritizes and reflects on DEI through a regular review of project policies and performance. This reflection is documented in the following DEI.md file based on specific [CHAOSS project](https://chaoss.community) DEI metrics.

### [Project Access](https://chaoss.community/?p=4953)

Project access is addressed in our project through various efforts. Through these efforts, we aim to support access for all. Specific efforts in our project include:

{{if .ProjectAccess}}{{range .ProjectAccess}}- {{.}}
{{end}}{{else}}- *Sample — edit these to describe how your project addresses access.*
- All virtual meetings are transcribed, and members can join via computer or phone. Video is not required to participate.
- Virtual meetings are attentive to global time zones so members across regions can participate.
- Translation services are provided for project documentation where feasible.
- All areas of the project are open to community contributions.
{{end}}
### [Communication Transparency](https://chaoss.community/?p=4957)

Communication transparency is addressed in our project through a variety of different efforts. Through these efforts, we aim to support transparency for all. Specific efforts in our project include:

{{if .CommTransparency}}{{range .CommTransparency}}- {{.}}
{{end}}{{else}}- *Sample — edit these to describe how your project addresses communication transparency.*
- All project documentation is publicly available.
- Appropriate documentation is shared at the start of every working group meeting.
- Decisions that impact the project are shared across working groups and channels so members can participate in the process.
- Any information that cannot be made public is marked as internal and listed by name.
{{end}}
### [Newcomer Experiences](https://chaoss.community/?p=4891)

The newcomer experience is addressed in our project through a variety of different efforts. Through these efforts, we aim to support the newcomer experience for all new members. Specific efforts in our project include:

{{if .NewcomerExperiences}}{{range .NewcomerExperiences}}- {{.}}
{{end}}{{else}}- *Sample — edit these to describe how your project addresses the newcomer experience.*
- Newcomer events and office hours are held regularly, open to all with an interest.
- A quick start guide for newcomers is available through the project navigation.
- First-time contributors are identified so reviewers can better assist them.
- Contributor documentation includes a walkthrough for making a first contribution.
{{end}}
### [Inclusive Leadership](https://chaoss.community/?p=3522)

Inclusive leadership is addressed in our project through a variety of different efforts. Through these efforts, we aim to support leadership opportunities for project members with an interest. Specific efforts in our project include:

{{if .InclusiveLeadership}}{{range .InclusiveLeadership}}- {{.}}
{{end}}{{else}}- *Sample — edit these to describe how your project addresses inclusive leadership.*
- Our governance document is reviewed on a regular basis to identify roles that guide the project's direction.
- Working group meetings provide the opportunity to be led by different people at each meeting.
- The project ensures a diverse candidate slate when selecting new maintainers.
- One or more maintainers participate in DEI group meetings or events.
{{end}}
